Subject: ps2xRecomp: VU0 macro loads/stores in VU0 memory, VSQI/VSQD operands, vi0 fixed at 0, VCALLMSR from CMSAR0

Rule of Rose port, audit after 0013 (VU0 registers the hardware fixes or protects):
- VSQI/VSQD took fs from bits 20-16 and it from bits 15-11 (VLQI/VLQD's order); the EE manual has fs = 15-11,
  it = 20-16. The skinning routine 0x227598 saves vf16-vf23 with `vsqi vfN, (vi1++)`: it stored vf1 at
  vi[16..23] (past the 16-entry VI array, whose increments then changed Q/P/I) and its restore loaded garbage.
- VLQI/VSQI/VLQD/VSQD/VILWR/VISWR addressed EE memory 0x0-0x3ff0 instead of VU0 data memory, which the VU0
  microprograms (VCALLMS) read; VILWR/VISWR also ignored the field's word offset. Now a quadword index into
  VU0 data memory (4 KB, wrapping), the field selecting the word.
- The VI register stepped as `& 0x3FF`; it is a 16-bit register.
- vi0 is hardwired to 0 like vf0: a translation that writes ctx->vi[0] is followed by restoring it.
- VCALLMSR read ctx->vi[27] (past the array): it starts the microprogram at CMSAR0 (control register 27).

diff --git a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/code_generator.cpp b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/code_generator.cpp
--- a/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/code_generator.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/code_generator.cpp
@@ -75,6 +75,15 @@
         return code;
     }
 
+    // vi0 is hardwired to 0 as well: any translation that writes it (VIADD/VISUB/VIAND/VIOR/VIADDI/VMTIR/VILWR with
+    // destination vi0, a load/store's address update on vi0) is followed by restoring it.
+    static std::string keepVi0Zero(std::string code)
+    {
+        if (code.find("ctx->vi[0] = ") != std::string::npos)
+            code += " ctx->vi[0] = 0;";
+        return code;
+    }
